 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How have you been? Try riding it in the middle instead at the edge where you had the jump. Also, check that the sprockets aren't worn or missing teeth. You' up first. Don't worry, it's yours again. Start fresh fire from scratch, and use it mainly outdoors for a few nights to be sure it' stable before using it for warmth and sleeping. With the fire, turn it the other way, so it helps rather than wins. With a chain, turning it to go back is normal. Then it' time for a chain replacement. You can do it yourself if you' cleaned it well, or take it into a bike shop.",
